From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Owen O'Hehir <40183643+OOHehir@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 17:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rk3506: recipe-track M2/M3 rk3506_common.h memory-map edits

This makes durable two previously build-tree-ONLY edits to
include/configs/rk3506_common.h that were never recipe-tracked (a
clean `bitbake -c clean`/`-c cleansstate` would have silently
regressed M2). Both are folded here so SRC_URI is the single
source of truth.

(NOTE: the RKIMG_BOOTCOMMAND `run distro_bootcmd;` reorder is
already carried by 0001-rk3506-add-distro-boot-fallback.patch and
is deliberately NOT duplicated here.)

1. M2 (2026-05-15) CONFIG_SYS_TEXT_BASE 0x00200000 -> 0x00400000.
   U-Boot linked at 0x200000 placed its pre-relocation vector /
   link-addr refs inside OP-TEE's live secure TEE_RAM
   [0x00001000,0x00201000), wedging the non-secure world on the
   first exception (SWD-confirmed). 0x400000 is clear of TEE_RAM,
   the FDT and INIT_SP, and matches the FIT `uboot` load +
   OP-TEE CFG_NS_ENTRY_ADDR so link==load==entry. This is the
   load-bearing M2-PASS fix; its own in-tree comment had flagged
   "proper Yocto recipe patch = M6 item" -- done here at M3.

2. M3 (2026-05-16) ENV_MEM_LAYOUT relocation. Vendor U-Boot
   2017.09 jumps to the raw zImage at kernel_addr_c; it does not
   decompress. The ARM kernel CONFIG_AUTO_ZRELADDR self-
   decompressor then targets (PC & 0xf8000000) + 0x8000. With the
   stock kernel_addr_c=0x01100000 (< 0x08000000) that resolved to
   0x00008000, straight through the OP-TEE secure window which the
   M2 DDR-firewall + SGRF fix makes non-secure-INACCESSIBLE -- so
   the NS decompressor external-aborted and cpu0 tight-looped at
   PA ~0x7bcd42 with no console (M3 hang, optee-rk3506 JOURNAL
   2026-05-15 19:30 / 2026-05-16 17:05). kernel_addr_c/_r raised
   to 0x08000000 so AUTO_ZRELADDR resolves to 0x08008000 -- clear
   of the secure window and below the SHMEM 0x10000000 mask
   boundary. fdt_addr_r (was 0x00063000, inside the secure window)
   and ramdisk_addr_r moved above the decompress + self-relocation
   scratch, both kept < 0x10000000. Kernel-side counterparts
   (reserved-memory growth, ramoops move, maxcpus=1) are in the
   Lyra Ultra board DTS.

Signed-off-by: Owen O'Hehir <40183643+OOHehir@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/include/configs/rk3506_common.h b/include/configs/rk3506_common.h
index db22b34b12..1b84fbab4d 100644
--- a/include/configs/rk3506_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/rk3506_common.h
@@ -14,7 +14,19 @@
 #define COUNTER_FREQUENCY		24000000
 #define CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_LEN		(16 << 20)
 #define CONFIG_SYS_CBSIZE		1024
-#define CONFIG_SYS_TEXT_BASE		0x00200000
+/*
+ * M2 (2026-05-15): 0x00200000 -> 0x00400000. Upstream OP-TEE's
+ * secure TEE_RAM is a fixed 2 MB CORE_MMU_PGDIR granule
+ * [0x1000,0x201000); U-Boot linked at 0x200000 put its
+ * pre-relocation vector base / link-addr refs inside OP-TEE's
+ * live secure RAM, wedging NS on the first exception
+ * (SWD-confirmed, JOURNAL 2026-05-15 19:00/19:25). 0x400000 is
+ * clear of TEE_RAM, the FDT (~0x2a61c8) and INIT_SP (0x600000);
+ * matches the FIT `uboot` load + OP-TEE CFG_NS_ENTRY_ADDR (both
+ * 0x400000) so link==load==entry. Build-tree edit for the
+ * bring-up flash loop; proper Yocto recipe patch = M6 item.
+ */
+#define CONFIG_SYS_TEXT_BASE		0x00400000
 #define CONFIG_SYS_INIT_SP_ADDR		0x00600000
 #define CONFIG_SYS_LOAD_ADDR		0x00008000
 #define CONFIG_SYS_BOOTM_LEN		(64 << 20)	/* 64M */
@@ -58,18 +70,38 @@
 #define CONFIG_PREBOOT
 
 /*
- *     fdt:  396K - 524K
- *   Image:  1M+32k - 16M
- *  zImage:  16M - 24M
- * ramdisk:  24M - ...
+ * M3 (2026-05-16): relocated clear of OP-TEE secure TEE_RAM.
+ * OP-TEE's secure window is [0x00001000,0x00201000); the M2
+ * DDR-firewall + SGRF fix makes it NS-INACCESSIBLE (aborts on any
+ * NS touch). Vendor U-Boot 2017.09 does NOT decompress the kernel
+ * — it jumps to the raw zImage at kernel_addr_c. The ARM kernel
+ * self-decompressor (CONFIG_AUTO_ZRELADDR) then lands the image at
+ * (PC & 0xf8000000) + 0x8000. With kernel_addr_c < 0x08000000 that
+ * resolved to 0x00008000 — straight through the secure window — so
+ * the NS decompressor aborted (cpu0 tight-loop @ 0x7bcd42, JOURNAL
+ * 2026-05-15 19:30 / 2026-05-16 17:05). Raising kernel_addr_c/_r to
+ * 0x08000000 makes AUTO_ZRELADDR resolve to 0x08008000 — clear of
+ * the secure window AND of SHMEM [0x10000000,0x10080000) (the next
+ * 128 MB mask boundary, 0x10000000, is deliberately NOT crossed).
+ * fdt/ramdisk moved above the decompress + self-reloc scratch and
+ * kept < 0x10000000. Memory < 0x08000000 (incl. OP-TEE) falls
+ * below the kernel's detected PHYS_OFFSET and is harmlessly
+ * ignored. Reserved-memory / ramoops / maxcpus counterparts live
+ * in meta-rockchip-rk3506/recipes-kernel/linux/files/
+ * rk3506b-luckfox-lyra-ultra.dts. RAM-waste optimisation (relocate
+ * OP-TEE high so the kernel can use 0x8000 again) is an M4+/M6 item.
+ *     fdt:  208M
+ *   Image:  128M+32k - ~176M
+ *  zImage:  128M (entry; self-relocates)
+ * ramdisk: 224M
  */
 #define ENV_MEM_LAYOUT_SETTINGS \
 	"scriptaddr=0x00b00000\0"	\
 	"pxefile_addr_r=0x00c00000\0"	\
-	"fdt_addr_r=0x00063000\0"	\
-	"kernel_addr_r=0x00108000\0"	\
-	"kernel_addr_c=0x01100000\0"	\
-	"ramdisk_addr_r=0x01800000\0"
+	"fdt_addr_r=0x0d000000\0"	\
+	"kernel_addr_r=0x08000000\0"	\
+	"kernel_addr_c=0x08000000\0"	\
+	"ramdisk_addr_r=0x0e000000\0"
 
 #include <config_distro_bootcmd.h>
 
--
2.42.0
